**Chain I survives.** No countermodel was found for a Keller self-map of \(\mathbb{C}^2\).

- **NO-CUSP-PREIMAGE** and **CUSP-A-VOID** hold on the listed hypotheses (properness over the complement, local-to-global \(\pi_1\) surjectivity from the cone, smoothness of \(E\), disjoint components, \(\chi\) additivity, \(\mathbb{C}[t]^*=\mathbb{C}^*\)).
- The \(N\)-fold cover of \(\mathbb{C}^2\) minus a cone curve exists as an abstract Stein surface with \(\chi=0\) (the 26 survivors are such covers). It is refused as an open of \(\mathbb{C}^2\) at Euler characteristic, at \(\pi_1\), and at \(\mathbb{A}^1\to\mathbb{C}^*\).
- Lin–Zaidenberg (Soviet Math. Dokl. 28 (1983) 200–204): there is no non-quasihomogeneous unicuspidal curve homeomorphic to \(\mathbb{C}\) in \(\mathbb{C}^2\) over \(\mathbb{C}\). The \(\mathbb{C}^*\)-retraction is not an extra assumption. GATE’s Invent. Math. 68 (1982) citation is the wrong paper.
- A smooth \(\mathbb{A}^1\) cannot pass over the cusp (the germ of \(E\) would be a \((p,q)\)-cusp). The fibre over the cusp is empty: a local section of a connected \(N\)-sheeted cover of the punctured ball forces \(N=1\).

**Prop. 6.1.** The charged MPRIME text supports Reading A: \(a_p\) is the affine fibre of the cusp and equals 1, putting a point of \(E\) over \(c\). Instantiating that with NO-CUSP-PREIMAGE gives \(0=-1\) in \((M')\) and in \((L)+(K)\). That is another emptiness proof, not a rescue of case (A). CUSP-KILL’s \(y_0\) construction is not an independent geometric step.

